From 03fc2987cf78b4a7b58f1bbf4026d702af0304cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 04:41:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09636/11362] [outer-loop] Widen four guards per QA-layer
 SILENT_NON_FIRING findings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each finding named a real input its guard was supposed to catch and did
not; each is widened (not rewritten) with the named input as a test.

1. substrate_alias_evidence_lint: ALIAS_RE anchors on the quote PAIR so
   'local_python_no_llm' single-quoted is caught; a prose apostrophe
   cannot open a match (negative test).
2. test_suite_mutation_check: the pre-commit stash window — a
   stash-hidden path counts as dirty for marker retirement; refusal
   names it [stash-hidden] and warns against checkout in the window.
   Reads only; nothing is reverted; freshness bounds the refusal.
3. operator_curated_docs_lint: --name-status, BOTH sides of R/C, so
   R100 README.md -> docs/archive/project-intro.md is caught on its
   protected SOURCE. Module docstring gains its REQ-ARC-WMTE-6042
   trace (the spec-coverage hook surfaced the pre-existing gap the
   first time anyone touched the file).
4. operator_curated_doc_guard: allow_relative derives from the event's
   dir_fd (-1/None = AT_FDCWD = CWD-relative; a real fd keeps the
   rmtree protection). Closes os.replace(tmp, 'README.md') with dst
   dirfd -1, and the unlink shape.

Mutations RED->GREEN x5; 134 tests across the four suites; the rmtree
false-fire regression stayed green under every mutation.
PRE_COMMIT_HOME sandboxed in the mutation-check fixture so tests never
read the operator's live pre-commit cache.

